===Climate===
[[File:Naruto Inland Sea.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The calm waters of the Seto Inland Sea near Geisei, with the Naruto Islands visible in the distance.]]

Naruto Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification ''Cfa''), moderated by the surrounding ocean waters. The Seto Inland Sea coast enjoys a particularly mild climate with low rainfall relative to the rest of Sanzu, sheltered by the surrounding mountains from the worst of the typhoon season. The mountainous interior receives significantly higher precipitation, particularly during the summer monsoon.

The Naruto Strait creates a unique microclimate along the northern coast, where the rapid tidal flow generates frequent sea mists and cooler summer temperatures. The contrast between the mild Inland Sea coast and the cooler, wetter mountain interior has shaped the prefecture's agricultural patterns, with citrus and sudachi cultivation concentrated along the coast and forestry dominating the uplands.

